---
components: ["Gantt"]
description: A Gantt chart shows tasks as bars on a time axis beside a hierarchical task list, with progress, milestones, summaries, dependencies, and bars that can be moved and resized with a pointer or the keyboard.
---

## Basic

Create a chart with `tasks` and `links`. A task is a [TreeViewGrid](/components/TreeViewGrid) node with dates: `start` and `end` are `Date` objects or `YYYY-MM-DD` strings, and `end` is the last day of the task, so a task that starts and ends on the same day takes one day. A task with `nodes` is a summary: its bar spans its children and its progress is theirs, weighted by length. Set `milestone` for a diamond on `start`, and `progress` (0 to 100) to fill a bar. A task without `start` has a row and no bar.

A link is `{ from, to }`: the task `to` starts after `from` finishes. The line is dashed and red when the successor starts on or before the last day of its predecessor.

Use `Gantt` when the dates are the point. For rows that share columns and have no time axis, use [TreeViewGrid](/components/TreeViewGrid). For flat records, use [DataTable](/components/DataTable).

<FileSource src="/framed/Gantt/Gantt" />

## Time axis

### Zoom

Set `zoom` to `"day"`, `"week"`, `"month"` or `"quarter"`. The header has two tiers: months over days or weeks, and years over months or quarters. Headers come from `Intl`, so `locale` sets the language, the first day of the week, and which days are the weekend. Weekends are shaded where a day is wide enough to see (day and week zoom). The today line sits at the current day; set `today` to pin it, or to `false` to hide it. Set `rangeStart` and `rangeEnd` to fix the span of the axis. By default it runs from a week before the first task to a week after the last.

<FileSource src="/framed/Gantt/GanttZoom" />

### Locale

Set `locale` on the server as well as the client. Its default is `"en"`, not the browser's language, so a server render and the hydrated page agree. `Intl` has no format for a quarter, so `formatQuarter` makes the label.

<FileSource src="/framed/Gantt/GanttLocale" />

## Sizes

Set `size` to control row height. The list and the bars share it, so they stay on the same rows. The sizes are the same as [DataTable](/components/DataTable#sizes).

| Size | Alias | Height |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `"compact"` | `"xs"` | 24px |
| `"short"` | `"sm"` | 32px |
| `"medium"` | `"md"` | 40px |
| unset | `"lg"` | 48px |
| `"tall"` | `"xl"` | 64px |

<FileSource src="/framed/Gantt/GanttSizes" />

## Task list

The list is a [TreeViewGrid](/components/TreeViewGrid). By default it has Task, Start and End columns; a summary shows the dates it derives from its children. Set `headers` for other columns and `listWidth` for the width. The list stays in view while it takes at most half of the chart's width. In a narrower chart, such as on a phone, it scrolls away with the timeline. A column reads the task field of the same `key`, and `display` formats it.

The list does not wrap text, since a cell that grows taller than the row would push the list out of line with the bars. Text that does not fit ends in an ellipsis, and the cell shows the full text on hover.

<FileSource src="/framed/Gantt/GanttColumns" />

## Editing

Drag a bar to move it, or drag either end to change its first or last day. Dates snap to a day at day and week zoom and to a week at month and quarter zoom. The bar shows the new dates while you drag, and the task is written when you let go. Press <DocKbd label="Escape" /> to cancel a drag.

The `change` event fires before the write and is cancelable. Its detail is `{ id, start, end, previous, mode, source }`, with `start` and `end` in the same kind as the task holds, a `Date` or a string. Call `preventDefault()` to keep the task as it is. Otherwise the chart writes the new dates into `tasks`, so bind `tasks` to receive them. The chart never moves other tasks: a successor that now starts too early is drawn dashed, and a listener can shift it from the same event.

A summary, a task with `readonly: true`, and every task when `readonly` is set on the chart cannot be moved. A task with `disabled: true` is drawn as disabled and takes no pointer or focus, as its row in the list does not.

<FileSource src="/framed/Gantt/GanttChange" />

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Bind `tasks`, or write the dates yourself in a `change` listener | The chart writes only when the event is not canceled, and only into its own `tasks`. |
| Cancel the event to enforce a rule, such as no start before a deadline | A canceled change leaves the bar where it was, with no flicker. |
| Keep `start` and `end` in one kind, strings or dates | The event returns the kind the task holds. |
| Don't edit a summary's dates | They derive from the children. Change a child. |

## Keyboard

The list is a treegrid with one tab stop. The bars are a second tab stop: <DocKbd label="Tab" /> enters the timeline at the last focused bar, or the first. <DocKbd label="←" /> and <DocKbd label="→" /> swap in right-to-left layouts, where <DocKbd label="←" /> moves a task later.

| Focus on | Key | Action |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bar | <DocKbd label="→" /> / <DocKbd label="←" /> | Move the task one day later or earlier (one week at month and quarter zoom). |
| Bar | <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + <DocKbd label="→" /> / <DocKbd label="←" /> | Move the last day later or earlier. |
| Bar | <DocKbd label="Alt" /> + <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + <DocKbd label="→" /> / <DocKbd label="←" /> | Move the first day later or earlier. |
| Bar | <DocKbd label="↑" /> / <DocKbd label="↓" /> | Focus the previous or next bar. Rows without a bar and disabled tasks are skipped. |
| Bar | <DocKbd label="Home" /> / <DocKbd label="End" /> | Focus the first or last bar. |
| Bar | <DocKbd label="Enter" /> / <DocKbd label="Space" /> | Select the task's row. |

A milestone moves but does not resize. A summary and a locked task take no arrow keys.

## Accessibility

A screen reader gets a bar's dates from its name, not from the axis, which is hidden. The bar is a focusable `button` whose name is the task, its kind, its dates, its progress and the tasks it follows: "Design review, Mar 9 – 13, 2026, 60% complete, after Write the brief". The dates come from `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, so `locale` and `dateFormat` set their language and shape. Set `barLabel` to write the name yourself, and `hintText` for the hint that a bar can be moved.

The task list is also a table of the same data, with a Start and an End column for each row, so the dates are available without the bars. A keyboard change is announced in a live region. The dependency lines are decoration: they are hidden from assistive technology, and the name carries what they show.

## Right-to-left

Time runs from the inline start to the inline end, as the rest of the layout does: under `dir="rtl"` the list is on the right and later dates are further left. The links are drawn for left-to-right and mirrored, so they follow the bars. Drag direction and the arrow keys follow the layout.

## Forced colors and print

In forced colors every bar has a border, progress is a system-color fill, the milestone and summary are solid, the links keep their stroke, and the timeline keeps its row lines. A dashed link marks a conflict by its dashes, not its color. Selection is a thicker `Highlight` border. When printed the chart is as wide as its axis, with nothing sticky or scrolling; choose a zoom whose axis fits the page.
